  m_Name: Dilema_BrtOuViaduto
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Demanda induzida
  _titleEn: Induced demand
  _category: 1
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Quando fica mais f\xE1cil dirigir, mais gente dirige. Por isso, ampliar
    vias raramente resolve o congestionamento por muito tempo: o espa\xE7o novo atrai
    carros novos."
  _summaryEn: 'When driving gets easier, more people drive. That is why adding road
    space rarely fixes congestion for long: new capacity attracts new cars.'
  _realWorld: "Duranton e Turner viram, em cidades dos EUA, que a quilometragem dirigida
    cresce na propor\xE7\xE3o das vias. Em Seul, a via elevada de Cheonggyecheon
    (168 mil carros por dia) foi demolida a partir de 2003."
  _realWorldEn: Duranton and Turner found, in US cities, that vehicle kilometers
    grow in proportion to roads. In Seoul, the elevated Cheonggyecheon road (168,000
    cars a day) was torn down starting in 2003.
  _tradeOffs: "O mesmo estudo n\xE3o viu o transporte coletivo reduzir o tr\xE1fego
    de carros. O corredor prioriza o \xF4nibus, mas tira espa\xE7o de quem dirige."
  _tradeOffsEn: The same study found transit did not reduce car traffic. A corridor
    prioritizes buses but takes space from drivers.
  _sources:
  - Label: Duranton e Turner, The Fundamental Law of Road Congestion (NBER)
    Url: https://www.nber.org/papers/w15376
  - Label: Revitalizing a City by Reviving a Stream (ADB)
    Url: https://www.development.asia/case-study/revitalizing-city-reviving-stream
